{"causation_id":null,"correlation_id":"issue-226-acceptance-ledger-unit-f4607a8b","event_hash":"741b14d2b211bfe06f35bbc9c12a93e6c0ed56ae228f839a0819aa8d0428c666","event_id":"c71841b5-f26c-48e6-a296-3cf0e5ede565","event_schema_version":1,"payload":{"feature":"ISSUE #226 — ACCEPTANCE LEDGER UNIT 1, one narrow visit. Branch slice-dsh-8810, stacked on slice-dsh-pass-d (PR #326); adopt every commit.\n\nThe ledger openspec/changes/2026-09-09-226-session-resumption/acceptance-ledger-8.8-8.10.md maps every acceptance clause of tasks 8.8 and 8.10 to opened evidence and lists the remaining work as narrow units in dependency order. READ its sections 5 and 6 FIRST. You do exactly ONE unit, verbatim below, and nothing else; the units before yours have landed on this branch where they come earlier in the order 1, 2a, 2b, 2c, 3, 4a.\n\nYOUR UNIT, verbatim from the ledger:\n\n1. **Assert the adaptation's delta digest.** Closes A67 and B99 (the one of\n   five sub-obligations now open). Touches\n   `crates/brokkr-protocol/src/adapters/composite/tests.rs` only, inside\n   `the_committed_plugin_set_is_the_six_files_and_the_one_expression_delta`.\n   Proof: recompute SHA-256 over `lib/index.js:253\\n`, the upstream line\n   prefixed `-`, the adapted line prefixed `+`, each newline-terminated, and\n   assert equality with `PROVENANCE.md`'s `78256d2e…`; show the assertion\n   binds by changing either line in the expectation and observing it part.\n   No production change; `extensions/` stays byte-identical.\n\nRULES. Stay inside the files your unit names. Tests assert exact reasons and exact values, never is_err(); every new test is shown to bind by a compiling mutation that makes it fail, then restored, and you record the failing test name and assertion. Fixtures build on a canonicalised temporary root; no test reads .forge/ or needs an installed provider. If your unit says a failure on current production bytes is a production finding, STOP and report it as your result instead of adjusting the test. Hosts are Linux and macOS only (decision 0063). Keep the session small: commit when the unit is done.\n\nGATES, crate-scoped: cargo fmt --all -- --check; cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings; the suite of each crate you touched. Do not run the exact coverage script or tick any checkbox: those are later units. Record in the ledger's section 6, under your unit, one dated line saying what landed and the commit. Frozen contracts, policy/phase-machine.json, fixtures/, reference/, extensions/ and docs/decisions/ do not move; 0056 stays proposed; the DSH route stays disabled.","manifest":{"agents":{"analyze:judge":{"adapter_digest":"9978453a32fbe613db3c58b618e0027009458800773b80ce3841c21f80fd61d8","agent":"gpt-flash-analyst","agent_digest":"47c760b694564f7b768a05638b5b9b4d48b15b4c64e8a45350c3ba1a3c5e9370","chain":["astra"],"charter_digest":"964414f4d6e6f4bc871e793707197eb38b3aa6005051fe5012187a160d1f44e0","chosen_index":0,"model":"astra","notices":[],"provider":"codex","skipped":[]},"clarify:judge":{"adapter_digest":"9978453a32fbe613db3c58b618e0027009458800773b80ce3841c21f80fd61d8","agent":"gpt-flash-clarifier","agent_digest":"69affde99c5f43a9c69bdf0b01a1be37534428bf73d8b3da8fb4aa6675b91c60","chain":["astra"],"charter_digest":"5028f0624c92272ce12a4cc50fd771e86591436dd912d31b2127687a3d233fa7","chosen_index":0,"model":"astra","notices":[],"provider":"codex","skipped":[]},"design:chief":{"adapter_digest":"9978453a32fbe613db3c58b618e0027009458800773b80ce3841c21f80fd61d8","agent":"gpt-flash-chief-architect","agent_digest":"34531e4ef643bbf5eccf42dd3263878c262d593b4916a5b2c20c5249d8fea96b","chain":["astra"],"charter_digest":"c6d224031f2e18010fc5e104cf4692fe7c51713e9c43da9f89f748331f4a69da","chosen_index":0,"model":"astra","notices":[],"provider":"codex","skipped":[]},"design:positions:robustness":{"adapter_digest":"9978453a32fbe613db3c58b618e0027009458800773b80ce3841c21f80fd61d8","agent":"gpt-flash-position-robustness","agent